{
 "topic": "de.grain-first-dimensional-design",
 "voice": "breeze-mellow-v2",
 "asr": "large-v3-turbo",
 "clips": {
  "01": {
   "hash": "3e7cdf070909e046",
   "takes": [
    "f111ea50efddbe937990",
    "b82396f4dc7a7f0f02e6"
   ],
   "duration": 14.09,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The exact same order, kept two different ways.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.458
    },
    {
     "text": "One keeps a single row for the whole thing. The other keeps one row per line inside it. Ask which product actually sold, and only one of them can even answer.",
     "start": 3.878,
     "end": 13.74
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 166,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02": {
   "hash": "1dcde0b731cd6bbf",
   "takes": [
    "2dbf9be403530ebe2892",
    "872bcd245d3103b8dfe5"
   ],
   "duration": 13.019,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Four decisions, always made in the same order.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.324
    },
    {
     "text": "What business process. What one row of the result represents. What it's broken down by. And what's actually being measured.",
     "start": 3.744,
     "end": 12.669
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 129,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03": {
   "hash": "1ef099bfe1caca2e",
   "takes": [
    "bcd02bfefa0f18ebdffd",
    "b593d0d3a9475a3de59e"
   ],
   "duration": 13.682,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That second decision is the one everything else depends on.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.262
    },
    {
     "text": "Deciding what a single row represents has to happen before anything else, because every later choice has to agree with it.",
     "start": 4.682,
     "end": 13.332
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 136,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04": {
   "hash": "8c291296961540ec",
   "takes": [
    "5a60559cf5b6a5715874",
    "8d283b01180b1e71fc64"
   ],
   "duration": 11.106,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's where that gets decided for real.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 2.778
    },
    {
     "text": "An order and its line items need one fact table. Should one row be the whole order, or just one of its lines?",
     "start": 3.198,
     "end": 10.756
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.1,
   "true_peak": -2.6,
   "wpm": 162,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04a": {
   "hash": "2fbcceffa9d40587",
   "takes": [
    "395a1a408ba5b92b8490",
    "63da3531d94becd8096e"
   ],
   "duration": 10.9,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "One of its lines. That's the most basic unit this process actually produces.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.452
    },
    {
     "text": "The order itself is really just several of those added together.",
     "start": 5.872,
     "end": 10.55
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 132,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "05": {
   "hash": "e4362f9959c4fb4d",
   "takes": [
    "a84e737944c2afa277d3",
    "dbf41b39890a45e85712"
   ],
   "duration": 12.473,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's the proof, run for real.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 2.707
    },
    {
     "text": "Add up every line's own total, grouped however you like, and you land back on the exact order total every single time.",
     "start": 3.127,
     "end": 12.123
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 135,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06": {
   "hash": "f80694242274314e",
   "takes": [
    "0401748d869ec8fd2e98",
    "414d92c41f99c75bf409"
   ],
   "duration": 16.247,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now, here's what the other choice would actually have cost you.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.3
    },
    {
     "text": "A table kept at one row per whole order never had a column for which product, or how many, in the first place. Not a harder question. One it simply has no way to answer.",
     "start": 4.72,
     "end": 15.897
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 170,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "07": {
   "hash": "29bf8ce983a3a1c0",
   "takes": [
    "1a9b8869183bceb69cb7",
    "bfd82aa08a1886e2faa5"
   ],
   "duration": 10.527,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's the first kind, of three you'll run into.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.101
    },
    {
     "text": "This one adds up correctly no matter how you slice it, and that was just checked directly, not assumed.",
     "start": 3.521,
     "end": 10.177
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 160,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08": {
   "hash": "57c3128c5c80a434",
   "takes": [
    "3a50607a8e4b06c45563",
    "84e637974ba846f9d98c"
   ],
   "duration": 12.746,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's the second kind, tested the same way.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.105
    },
    {
     "text": "A balance adds up fine across different accounts. Does it add up the same way across different stretches of time for the same account?",
     "start": 3.525,
     "end": 12.396
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 151,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08a": {
   "hash": "cdf65ca3a11adabd",
   "takes": [
    "6d4c5933bb2139021470",
    "ef5efeeccff67ced8082"
   ],
   "duration": 12.867,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "No. Adding up several time periods' balances gives you a number that means nothing at all.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.433
    },
    {
     "text": "The real year-end figure is just whatever the last period's own balance happened to be.",
     "start": 6.853,
     "end": 12.517
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 149,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "09": {
   "hash": "471b9e9dd3e319f4",
   "takes": [
    "6f6d1750188aa3c35065",
    "7824dd4fef900688c206"
   ],
   "duration": 16.324,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Watch that happen with real numbers.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 2.834
    },
    {
     "text": "Four quarters' balances, added together, land on a total with no meaning. The actual year-end balance was simply the fourth quarter's own number, sitting there the whole time.",
     "start": 3.254,
     "end": 15.974
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 129,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "10": {
   "hash": "275c1878ac4aa8e9",
   "takes": [
    "9a2fa1c6980f1ee640b4",
    "73567b5275b71aff0e01"
   ],
   "duration": 17.532,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now the third kind, and this one can't be added up at all, not even halfway.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.261
    },
    {
     "text": "Average two regions' profit margins the obvious way, and you get a different answer than if you add up their revenue and their cost separately first, and only then divide.",
     "start": 5.681,
     "end": 17.182
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.8,
   "wpm": 157,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "11": {
   "hash": "728752adf4c8f110",
   "takes": [
    "0981b4051375fda09b01",
    "f4c72ca29de12da905b5"
   ],
   "duration": 13.943,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's the actual fix, and it's simpler than it sounds.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.905
    },
    {
     "text": "Keep the pieces that do add up safely. Add those. Only compute the ratio at the very end, after the adding is already done.",
     "start": 4.325,
     "end": 13.593
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 146,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "12": {
   "hash": "89a686f79f2af8de",
   "takes": [
    "81995a2c534dfe0e4a30",
    "4d2035f08355351d3be6"
   ],
   "duration": 17.405,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Four decisions, in order, with the second one binding everything after it.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.276
    },
    {
     "text": "One kind of number adds up anywhere. One adds up almost anywhere, except across time. One doesn't add up at all, only its pieces do.",
     "start": 5.696,
     "end": 17.055
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 128,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "13": {
   "hash": "ffe6e1b2a44fe7b5",
   "takes": [
    "f1fb6c60ba513339aa39",
    "e143899f37745c171f69"
   ],
   "duration": 13.599,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Last one. A shipping cost, divided by how many units shipped.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.613
    },
    {
     "text": "Is it safe to just add that number up across orders, or does it need the same fix as the profit margin did?",
     "start": 6.033,
     "end": 13.249
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 150,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "13a": {
   "hash": "97e04807c15cfc22",
   "takes": [
    "533fa6133a16f9b84505",
    "49ecb560c41a77ac7eb8"
   ],
   "duration": 16.095,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The same fix. Add up the shipping cost and the unit count separately, then divide once at the end.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.804
    },
    {
     "text": "It's a ratio for exactly the same reason the margin was, so it breaks the same way if you add it up directly.",
     "start": 7.224,
     "end": 15.745
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.1,
   "true_peak": -2.7,
   "wpm": 157,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  }
 }
}